title: Go Out Resolves To Exiting
story: dungeo
description: ADR-268 acceptance 3 — `go out` resolves to exiting (D3 pair order), not going

---

# `go out` vs going — the only duplicate pattern with different actions in the
# standard grammar. ADR-268 D3: the exiting rule is defined earlier, so
# definition order decides the tie. Inside a vehicle, `go out` must exit the
# vehicle (exiting), not attempt the room's "out" exit (going).

## Setup - get lantern and navigate to the balloon
> gdt
[OK: contains "GDT ready"]

> tk brass lantern
[OK: contains "Taken"]

> ah Volcano Bottom
[OK: contains "Teleported"]

> ex
[OK: contains "Returning to game"]

> turn on lantern
[OK: contains "switches on"]

## Enter the balloon
> enter balloon
[OK: contains "You get into the balloon."]

## `go out` must resolve to exiting (climbing out of the vehicle)
> go out
[OK: contains "climb out of the balloon"]
